@startuml UseCaseDiagram

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

title Use Case Diagram

left to right direction

actor "Project Manager" as PM
actor "Port Authority Officer" as PAO
actor "Shipping Agent Representative" as SAR
actor "Logistics Operator" as LO

usecase "US2.1.1 - Set up the tools and infrastructure necessary to properly develop and manage the project" as UC2.1.1
usecase "US2.2.1 - Create and update vessel types" as UC2.2.1
usecase "US2.2.2 - Register and update vessel records" as UC2.2.2
usecase "US2.2.3 - Register and update docks" as UC2.2.3
usecase "US2.2.4 - Register and update storage areas" as UC2.2.4
usecase "US2.2.5 - Register new shipping agent organizations" as UC2.2.5
usecase "US2.2.6 - Register and manage representatives of a shipping agent organization" as UC2.2.6
usecase "US2.2.7 - Review pending Vessel Visit Notifications and approve or reject them" as UC2.2.7
usecase "US2.2.8 - Create/submit a Vessel Visit Notification" as UC2.2.8
usecase "US2.2.9 - Change / complete a Vessel Visit Notification while it is still in progress" as UC2.2.9
usecase "US2.2.10 - View the status of all my submitted Vessel Visit Notification" as UC2.2.10
usecase "US2.2.11 - Register and manage operating staff members" as UC2.2.11
usecase "US2.2.12 - Register and manage physical resources" as UC2.2.12
usecase "US2.2.13 - Register and manage qualifications" as UC2.2.13
usecase "US2.3.1 - Prepare a summary presentation of the client organization" as UC2.3.1
usecase "US2.3.2 - Analyze the organizational structure of the client" as UC2.3.2
usecase "US2.3.3 - Suggest improvements to the organization's internal structure or rules" as UC2.3.3
usecase "US2.3.4 - Identify and comment on the organization's values, vision, and mission" as UC2.3.4
usecase "US2.3.5 - Propose one SMART objective for each of the three management levels" as UC2.3.5
usecase "US2.3.6 - Conduct a SWOT analysis of the organization" as UC2.3.6
usecase "US2.3.7 - Propose a possible strategy for the organization" as UC2.3.7


PM --> UC2.1.1
PM --> UC2.3.1
PM --> UC2.3.2
PM --> UC2.3.3
PM --> UC2.3.4
PM --> UC2.3.5
PM --> UC2.3.6
PM --> UC2.3.7

PAO --> UC2.2.1
PAO --> UC2.2.2
PAO --> UC2.2.3
PAO --> UC2.2.4
PAO --> UC2.2.5
PAO --> UC2.2.6
PAO --> UC2.2.7

LO --> UC2.2.11
LO --> UC2.2.12
LO --> UC2.2.13

SAR --> UC2.2.8
SAR --> UC2.2.9
SAR --> UC2.2.10

@enduml